{"ts": "2026-08-09T13:34:30Z", "agent": "log-triage", "action": "query_metric", "detail": "sum by (service_name)(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total[10m])) -- frontend-proxy 16.574, frontend 16.219, flagd 11.500, frontend-web 6.815, product-catalog 6.374, cart 2.865, load-generator 2.167, image-provider 2.106, recommendation 1.374, checkout 0.833, currency 0.672, ad 0.570, quote 0.350, shipping 0.300, email 0.267, telemetry-docs 0.198, payment 0.137, flagd-ui 0.000 req/s", "reasoning": "Broad sweep before deciding anything looks off, and per lgtm-signal-gotchas I start with traces_span_metrics_calls_total rather than http_server_*/rpc_server_* because that family covers every service regardless of language (payment is Node.js and emits no http_server_* at all -- an empty result there would have been a metric-family gap, not health). This is also my traffic-alive check demanded by the correction: 18 services reporting, storefront path all non-zero."}
